How does he barcode scanner work?
## <!DOCTYPE html>
Tells the web browser that this file is a modern webpage.
## <html lang="en">
Starts the webpage and tells the computer the language used is English.
## <head>
Starts a hidden section for settings and links that the user cannot see on the screen.
## <meta charset="UTF-8">
Makes sure all letters, numbers, and symbols display correctly on the screen without turning into weird characters.
## <title>Library Self Checkout</title>
Sets the text that appears on the browser tab at the very top of your window.
## <script src="https://unpkg.com"></script>
Brings in the free scanner tool from the internet. This tool does all the hard math to read barcodes so you do not have to write it yourself.
## </head>
Closes the hidden settings section.
## <body>
Starts the visible section of the webpage where all the content lives.
## <h1>AOA Library Self Checkout</h1>
Displays a large, bold title text at the top of the webpage.
## <div id="scanner-view" style="width: 500px;"></div>
Creates an empty box on the screen that is 500 pixels wide. This is exactly where the webcam video feed will show up.
## <script>
Starts the section where we write JavaScript code to control how the scanner behaves.
## function onScanSuccess(decodedText, decodedResult) 
Creates a rule that says: "The exact millisecond a barcode is found, run the following action."
## alert("Scanned Code Data: " + decodedText);
Pops up a small alert window on the screen showing the numbers or text hidden inside the barcode and ends the success rule.
## const html5QrcodeScanner = new Html5QrcodeScanner(
Creates a brand new scanner setup.
## "scanner-view",
Tells the scanner to put the live webcam video inside the empty box we made earlier.
## { fps: 10, qrbox: 250 }
Tells the scanner to look at the camera 10 times every second, and draws a square target box on the screen to help the user aim the barcode.
## );
Finishes setting up the scanner choices.
## html5QrcodeScanner.render(onScanSuccess);
Asks the user for permission to use the webcam, turns the camera on, and starts looking for barcodes.
## </script>
Ends the JavaScript code section.
## </body>
Ends the visible section of the webpage.
## </html>
Ends the entire webpage file.


